3.1 **Folder layout (the only layout):**
```
public/images/hero/            hero.webp
public/images/trips/           trip_goa.webp trip_chikmagalur.webp trip_coorg.webp trip_gokarna.webp trip_hyderabad.webp
public/images/destinations/    dest_goa.webp dest_coorg.webp dest_chikmagalur.webp dest_gokarna.webp dest_hyderabad.webp
                               dest_kerala.webp dest_hampi.webp dest_meghalaya.webp dest_ooty.webp
public/images/stories/         story_gokarna_om.webp story_coorg_falls.webp story_chikmagalur_peak.webp
                               story_hyderabad_charminar.webp story_goa_beach.webp
public/images/sections/        stats_ocean.webp promo_mountain.webp
```
File name = registry key + extension (`.webp` preferred; `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.avif` accepted). Optional responsive variants: `<key>-480.webp`, `<key>-960.webp`, `<key>-1600.webp`. Paths in code are root-absolute (`/images/trips/trip_goa.webp`) because Vite serves `public/` at the site root and Vercel deploys it as-is. Add a `<link rel="preload" as="image" fetchpriority="high" imagesrcset=… imagesizes=…>` for the hero in `index.html` only if the hero file exists (generate it from the manifest, do not hard-code a missing path).

3.2 **Manifest generator** `scripts/generate-image-manifest.mjs` (plain Node ESM, no network). It scans `public/images/**`, matches files to registry keys by basename, reads intrinsic width/height (use the `image-size` devDependency) and byte size, groups `-480/-960/-1600` variants, and writes `src/data/image-manifest.generated.ts`:
```ts
export const imageManifest: Record<string, { src: string; srcSet?: string; width: number; height: number; bytes: number }> = { … };
```
Hook it as `"predev"`, `"prebuild"` and `"prelint"` in `package.json` so it always runs before `vite`/`tsc`. Commit the generated file (AI Studio and Vercel must work without extra steps). Output is deterministic (sorted keys).

3.3 **Registry** (`src/data/images.ts`): remove hand-set `status`. Each entry keeps `id`, `label`, `alt`, `objectPosition`, `aspect` (e.g. `"4/5"`), `sizes`, `accent`, `fallback`, plus **provenance** the owner must be able to audit:
```ts
provenance?: {
  kind: "owner" | "wikimedia-commons" | "other-licensed" | "ai-generated";
  title: string; author: string; sourceUrl: string; licence: string; licenceUrl: string;
  retrievedOn: string;          // ISO date
  verifiedSubject: string;      // one sentence: what you SAW in the pixels
  hotlinked?: boolean;          // true only under §5 step 2c
  commercialUseVerified: boolean;
}
```
`src`, `srcSet`, `width`, `height` come from `imageManifest[key]` merged in at module load. Derived state: `"photo"` if a manifest entry exists, otherwise `"missing"`. **No code path may mark an image as photo without a file.** Export `getImage(key)` that throws in dev and `console.error`s in prod for an unknown key.

3.4 **Validation scripts** (`package.json`): `"check:images": "node scripts/check-images.mjs"` and `"verify": "npm run lint && npm run check:images && npm run build && npm run test:browser"`.
`check-images.mjs` must: list every registry key and whether its file exists; fail on any `src` that does not resolve to a file; fail on any file in `public/images` not referenced by a key (orphans); warn >400 KB (hero >600 KB); fail if a file is <8 KB or has width <600 px (catches fakes); fail if width/height ratio differs from the registry `aspect` by more than 25 % (cropping-risk) unless an `objectPosition` is set; fail if a non-owner image lacks provenance or has `commercialUseVerified` undefined; fail if two keys map to byte-identical files (catches one photo reused as many); with `IMAGES_STRICT=1` (default for `npm run verify` and Vercel `buildCommand`) fail on **any missing key**. Without strict mode, missing keys print a loud table and exit 0 so a Studio preview still runs. Exit codes and output must be readable by a non-developer.

3.5 **Vercel:** add to `vercel.json` `"buildCommand": "IMAGES_STRICT=1 npm run check:images && npm run build"`, and long-cache headers for `/images/(.*)` (`Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` only if file names are content-hashed; otherwise `max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800`). Keep the SPA rewrite but **exclude `/images/` and `/assets/`** from it (`"source": "/((?!images/|assets/|.*\\..*).*)"`), so a missing image returns a real 404 instead of the HTML shell (which is what makes broken images look like a "loaded" 200 response).

